FEX: what i386 Android (32-bit bionic) needs under a guest base (SteamARM)

i386 programs of an Android 11 x86_64 image (dex2oat32, dalvikvm32,
app_process32 as zygote_secondary, the 32-bit HALs) all died under FEX's
32-bit mode on SteamARM's runtime; the i386 Steam client did not, because
it is glibc and brings FEX's VDSO thunk. MEASURED, one after the other
(SteamARM benchmarks/stage28-android-reliability.txt):

1. ELFCodeLoader: with no VDSO thunk, FEX makes a fallback vsyscall page
   (int 0x80; ret) with GuestMmap and a HOST mprotect, so its VMA tracking
   keeps the page as read-write: bionic calls AT_SYSINFO for every syscall
   and died at once, "NoExec instruction in entry block: F76AF000". The
   page is now tracked as executable (AddVirtualPage).
2. x32 futex: the guest-base syscall thunk bases every pointer-typed
   argument, and futex's fourth one is an integer for (CMP_)REQUEUE and
   WAKE_OP (val2): nr_requeue INT_MAX arrived negative, EINVAL, and ART
   aborted ("futex requeue failed for task queue condition").
3. x32 rt_sigtimedwait: a NULL siginfo (sigwait) hit FaultSafeUserMemAccess'
   "Unexpected nullptr syscall argument" (ART's signal catcher at exit); and
   an error (-errno, never -1) was copied out as a siginfo.
4. MemAllocator32Bit ignored mmap hints; Linux honours a free one. Under a
   guest base the window is the allocator's own and the bitset is the
   truth, so a free hint is taken. i386 ART's boot image is reserved at
   its link address: "Failed to mmap at expected address, mapped at
   0xee785000 instead of 0x70d32000", then an imageless start (6 s for a
   hello world; 1.6 s with the image).
5. x32 setsockopt/getsockopt dereferenced the guest's optval without the
   base (SO_RCVTIMEO_OLD/SO_SNDTIMEO_OLD, SO_ATTACH_FILTER): the zygote sets
   SO_RCVTIMEO on every connection and FEX faulted on 0xffff5ab0.

The binary carries the string "lxrt-i386-bionic" for SteamARM's tests.

diff --git a/Source/Tools/FEXInterpreter/ELFCodeLoader.h b/Source/Tools/FEXInterpreter/ELFCodeLoader.h
--- a/Source/Tools/FEXInterpreter/ELFCodeLoader.h
+++ b/Source/Tools/FEXInterpreter/ELFCodeLoader.h
@@ -666,6 +666,13 @@
         };
         memcpy(FEX::HLE::G2H(VSyscallPage), VSyscallCode, sizeof(VSyscallCode));
         mprotect(FEX::HLE::G2H(VSyscallPage), FEXCore::Utils::FEX_PAGE_SIZE, PROT_READ);
+        // The frontend decodes guest code only from ranges FEX's VMA tracking
+        // knows as executable, and the host mprotect above leaves this page
+        // recorded as the read-write anonymous mapping GuestMmap made: the
+        // first call through AT_SYSINFO (every syscall of i386 bionic, which
+        // uses it whenever it is set) died with "NoExec instruction in entry
+        // block" at this page. Track it as the executable page it is.
+        Handler->AddVirtualPage(Thread, reinterpret_cast<uint64_t>(VSyscallPage), FEXCore::Utils::FEX_PAGE_SIZE, PROT_READ | PROT_EXEC);
         VSyscallEntry = reinterpret_cast<uint64_t>(VSyscallPage);
       }
 
diff --git a/Source/Tools/LinuxEmulation/LinuxSyscalls/LinuxAllocator.cpp b/Source/Tools/LinuxEmulation/LinuxSyscalls/LinuxAllocator.cpp
--- a/Source/Tools/LinuxEmulation/LinuxSyscalls/LinuxAllocator.cpp
+++ b/Source/Tools/LinuxEmulation/LinuxSyscalls/LinuxAllocator.cpp
@@ -170,6 +170,29 @@
   // Check reserved range
   if (Fixed && PageAddr < 16) {
     return reinterpret_cast<void*>(-EINVAL);
+  }
+
+  // Linux places a mapping at its hint when the range there is free. Under a
+  // guest base the whole 4 GiB window is this allocator's own reservation and
+  // the bitset is the truth, so a free hint can be taken as a fixed mapping.
+  // i386 ART reserves its boot image at the address the image was built for
+  // and gives up on the image otherwise ("Failed to mmap at expected address,
+  // mapped at 0xee785000 instead of 0x70d32000", then an imageless start,
+  // 6 s for a hello world). A file mapping that must start on a host page
+  // (below) keeps the search when the hint is not on one.
+  if (!Fixed && Addr && GuestBase && PageAddr >= 16 && Addr + length <= (1ULL << 32) &&
+      !(fd != -1 && (offset & 0x3fff) == 0 && (G2H(Addr) & 0x3fff) != 0)) {
+    bool Free = true;
+    for (size_t i = 0; i < PagesLength; ++i) {
+      if (MappedPages.test(PageAddr + i)) {
+        Free = false;
+        break;
+      }
+    }
+    if (Free) {
+      flags |= MAP_FIXED;
+      Fixed = true;
+    }
   }
 
   if (!Fixed) {
